{"paper": "RRB-RPF-Constable-07-Mar-2025-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": false, "extracted_count": 120, "tagged_count": 33, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "A retailer buys an electronic item for ₹175. His overhead expenses are ₹25. He sells the electronic item for ₹320 and makes x%' profit. The value of x is:", "options": [{"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": "60"}, {"n": 2, "text": "The price of a car was ₹7,50,000 last year. The price increased by 15% this year. What is the price of the car this year?", "options": [{"text": "₹8,50,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹7,75,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹9,02,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹8,62,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": "₹8,62,500"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Ali ordered an LED screen from an online portal. The online portal allows two successive discounts of 12.5% and 25% on the marked price. If payment is made by credit card, there is another discount of 10% on the bill. If Ali made a payment of ₹59,062.50 by credit card, then the marked price of the LED screen is:", "options": [{"text": "₹1,02,500", "added": false}, {"text": "₹90,650", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,20,075", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "₹1,00,000"}, {"n": 4, "text": "Two trains of equal length are running on parallel lines in the same direction at speeds of 49 km/h and 31 km/h. The faster train passes the slower train in 42 seconds. The length of each train is:", "options": [{"text": "124 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "95 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "105 meters", "added": false}, {"text": "103 meters", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "train-vs-platform", "key_answer": "105 meters"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The sum of 8 numbers is 732. Find their average.", "options": [{"text": "91.5", "added": false}, {"text": "92.5", "added": false}, {"text": "90.5", "added": false}, {"text": "89.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "91.5"}, {"n": 6, "text": "Shifa can do a certain piece of work in 22 days. Shifa and Afiya can together do the same work in 18 days, and Shifa, Afiya and Mariyam can do the same work together in 9 days. In how many days can Shifa and Mariyam do the same work?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "The least multiple of 11, which leaves a remainder of 8, when divided by 5, 3, 18 and 20 is:", "options": [{"text": "1088", "added": false}, {"text": "1628", "added": false}, {"text": "908", "added": false}, {"text": "548", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "remainder", "key_answer": "1628"}, {"n": 8, "text": "Two banks, A and B, offered loans at 3.5% and 6% per annum, respectively. Vijay borrowed an amount of ₹400000 from each bank. Find the positive difference between the amounts of simple interest paid to the two banks by Vijay after 3 years.", "options": [{"text": "31500", "added": false}, {"text": "30000", "added": false}, {"text": "31000", "added": false}, {"text": "29500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": "30000"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Train A leaves station M at 6:20 AM and reaches station N at 3:20 PM on the same day. Train B leaves station N at 8:20 AM and reaches station M 